Hawaii this island paradise is one of  the most beautiful states in the Union  it's also the most reliably democratic  in 2012 President Barack Obama won the  state by a massive 42 percentage points  more than in any other state  Hawaii is such a Democratic stronghold  that its state Senate has only a single  sitting Republican an island on an  island who has the spacious minority  caucus room all to himself this is the  loneliest man in the Senate Aloha I'm  state senator Sam Slom I'm the leader of  the Senate minority in the Hawaii State  Legislature they refer to me as a lone  ranger but that's a good thing because  the lone Ranger's a good guy after the  election I started getting phone calls  sympathy messages and sympathy cards  about oh my gosh it's so sad that you're  the only one and as it turned out I had  my research staff look in the last 50  years this is the only example of a  single person of a major political party  of being in their house or their Senate  it's had many benefits first of all I  didn't have anybody trying to topple me  as a Minority Leader being a good  conservative libertarian it is an  individual that can do good things or  not-so-good things or whatever I'll be  sitting in a committee waiting to vote  and a committee clerk will come from  next door and say senator Slom senator  Slom we need you for a quorum whenever  there's a problem discovered or whatever  I'll go to the majority leadership and  tell them hey you know I know you're  gonna pass this bill I don't have the  votes to stop it obviously but you might  want to consider improving the bill and  passing a good bill frustrating to me is  the fact that normally they'll say yeah  fine we'll pass the bill this year we'll  come back next year and fix it my first  Senate speech ever was to my colleagues  when we had two Republicans at that time  I probably are not going to be able to  influence your votes most of the time  although I'll try but my point here is  I'm going to raise issues and talk about  unintended consequences so that years  later you will not have the luxury of  saying oh is that what that bill meant  is that what that does at least we'll  all know and you'll know why you're  voting forward or voting against it it's  interesting because the history of  which of course at one time was a  monarchy and then became a territory  Republicans ruled Hawaii completely for  50 years during territorial days and  then for the next 60 years it's been the  Democrats that have ruled completely  here's the thing  things are changing they're changing all  the time with the death of senior  senator Daniel Inouye last December who  had been in office for 54 years there  were generations that knew no one else  but him  there were even Republicans if they  wanted something done they went to Dan  Inouye he was the go-to it guy but now  he's gone and so some of the positions  that he blocked and some of the people  that he helped now there's more  independence of that Hawaii has been  positioned for a long time to take  advantage of you know outside investment  venture capital we could be a you know a  Singapore or a Hong Kong but we choose  not to because we have a long tradition  of government and government involvement  the basic change is going to come in  education we have charter schools as  part of the public school system I think  it's incumbent upon everyone  particularly people with children but  also people in business to be involved  in the schools of all the things that  you can do to be a change agent it's  educational choices I mean that's what  Milton Friedman stressed in Hawaii one  of the problems is we're 2,500 miles in  the middle of the ocean here unlike  other places on the mainland where you  could downsize if things got rough you  could move to you know a smaller  community or to another county or if you  had to cross the state lines in a way  basically you're here or you're not here  people want to be here but it's  expensive to be here and politically  it's expensive also  I am very supportive of the idea that we  can make changes here because if we  don't the the downside to all this is  being so far  in the Pacific the state will be far  lonelier than I am as the lone  Republican in the Senate
 

